	(footprint "cec-Connector_Blade:TE_63951-1_FASTON_Tab_250x032_RA_THT"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "7d811042-e792-4ee9-b130-2fb9eb7bbc2e")
		(at 13.86 14.65)
		(descr "TE Connectivity 63951-1 FASTON .250 right-angle (flat, in-plane) PC board tab -- TE dwg C=63951 rev L2, App Spec 114-2115. Blade 6.35mm+/-0.08 wide x 0.83/0.77mm thick lies FLAT/coplanar, extending +Y from the 2 THT legs (5.08mm+/-0.08 pitch, 1.40mm+/-0.05 dia holes -- same leg/hole pattern as the platform's existing TE_63849-1 straight tab). Local frame: origin at the leg-pair midpoint; +Y = the blade's reach direction (toward the board edge the blade hangs past once placed). Shoulder (near-leg) region measured +/-1.6mm off the datasheet's recurring 7.92mm shoulder/flange width (same value appears on the .187-series 1217061-1 and the straight 63849-1 -- tied to the shared leg geometry, not blade width, so it is reused here rather than re-derived); blade region tapers to the confirmed 6.35mm (+0.08 max = 6.43, rounded to 6.44 half-width margin) blade width from Y=+1.6 to the blade tip at Y=+8.89 (TE's own 'Profile Height from PCB' attribute for this part, read here as the blade's reach from the leg row -- flagged UNVERIFIED at the single-datum level pending a re-check against the raw vector drawing, per docs/standard-tier-review/blade-fit-check-2026-07-04.md addendum).")
